WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-GB

00:00:05.049 --> 00:00:06.430
Malcolm Grant&gt;&gt; Thank you very much.

00:00:06.430 --> 00:00:11.480
May we then move please to item 4 on the agenda,
which is the NHS Business Plan.

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:15.680
Simon has already raised the curtain, and
I will invite please Karen to speak to the

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:16.680
paper.

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:19.770
Karen Wheeler&gt;&gt; Thank you, Chair.

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:27.339
At the risk of repeating some of what Simon
has already talked about, today we published

00:00:27.339 --> 00:00:34.850
on our website the Business Plan for 2016/2017.

00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:43.739
This is of course a requirement for us to
publish the plan that reflects both our mandate,

00:00:43.739 --> 00:00:49.690
our accountabilities, our priorities, and
also how we are playing our role in supporting

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:56.579
the Five Year Forward View and the improvements
that we need to make across the system.

00:00:56.579 --> 00:01:03.660
We have made particular efforts this year
to try to make it simple, clear and very accessible

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:10.020
for all those who need to read it, and in
particular for our staff, so that they can

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:17.020
access it, read it and make sure that they
can how their work fits in to the overall

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:20.810
plan for the organisation.

00:01:20.810 --> 00:01:26.660
The plan has been through quite a lot of detailed
review, as you know, with our own Board members,

00:01:26.660 --> 00:01:37.980
stakeholders, DH and ministers, so it reflects
everybody’s views and comments.

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:44.290
There are accompanying documents to the plan,
which have a more granular detail about milestones,

00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:51.850
and we will be using those to track progress
through the year, but I did want to just draw

00:01:51.850 --> 00:01:55.590
out the key themes.

00:01:55.590 --> 00:02:00.500
We again have ten priorities, which largely
reflect the priorities that we had last year,

00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:06.490
so that we give continuity and stability to
the work we need to do, but also make sure

00:02:06.490 --> 00:02:13.220
that those same themes now are starting to
be much more about delivery rather than planning

00:02:13.220 --> 00:02:15.480
for change.

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:21.770
They line up against the Five Year Forward
View gaps, the three gaps: the health gap,

00:02:21.770 --> 00:02:25.180
the care gap and the finance and efficiency
gap.

00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:31.960
Under the health gap, we have themes and priorities
under cancer, mental health, learning disabilities

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:36.480
and type 2 diabetes prevention.

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:44.040
The care gap deals with primary care; urgent
and emergency care; elective and maternity,

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:51.319
implementing the maternity review; specialised
services; and commissioning changes in respect

00:02:51.319 --> 00:02:57.650
of new care models, integrated personalised
commissioning and increased choice.

00:02:57.650 --> 00:03:05.040
Then the final priority is around finance
and financial sustainability with underpinning

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:13.960
enablers, which are associated with the technology
enabler, to support all aspects of the plan;

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:21.980
how we empower patients and communities in
all we do and all of the changes that we are

00:03:21.980 --> 00:03:29.390
making, and how we focus on supporting leadership
across the system.

00:03:29.390 --> 00:03:34.209
The plan also sets out how we have allocated
resources according to those priorities, so

00:03:34.209 --> 00:03:42.569
that we are fully lined up and allocating
our funding according to those priorities.

00:03:42.569 --> 00:03:50.330
As I have said, we will be tracking delivery
programmes as we have done during the course

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:56.540
of this year, to make sure that, as far as
we can, we will deliver successfully to the

00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:58.660
commitments that are laid out in the plan.

00:03:58.660 --> 00:04:01.319
That is really all I wanted to say, Malcolm.

00:04:01.319 --> 00:04:03.400
Malcolm Grant&gt;&gt; Thank you very much, Karen.

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:08.060
The Board have been following the development
of the Business Plan over time, and I know

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:09.560
have been feeding into it.

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:13.140
We have a final version tabled with us this
morning.

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:24.219
May I now invite the Board to make any comments
or raise any queries with Karen and the team?

00:04:24.219 --> 00:04:31.229
Which suggests to me a general level of satisfaction,
and what the team have done is taken some

00:04:31.229 --> 00:04:34.270
probably quite conflicting comments from the
rest of the Board as the plan has developed,

00:04:34.270 --> 00:04:40.110
and converted them into something that has
found general consensus, true consensus, around

00:04:40.110 --> 00:04:41.110
the Board.

00:04:41.110 --> 00:04:44.340
We know that this is our formal response to
the government’s mandate.

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:49.509
We know also that we will be doing a lot of
other activity, some of which falls outside

00:04:49.509 --> 00:04:54.419
the Business Plan, simply because of events
as we go through the year, and other challenges.

00:04:54.419 --> 00:04:59.020
Can I then seek the formal approval of the
Board to the Business Plan?

00:04:59.020 --> 00:05:01.019
Good, thank you very much.

